1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,996
What if every blink skipped one second?

2
00:00:03,036 --> 00:00:04,567
You step off the curb,

3
00:00:04,607 --> 00:00:07,139
blink, and the bus that was far away

4
00:00:07,179 --> 00:00:09,353
is suddenly right in your face.

5
00:00:09,393 --> 00:00:11,281
Blink again, and it's gone.

6
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:13,877
Sports get strange.

7
00:00:13,917 --> 00:00:15,531
You throw a basketball,

8
00:00:15,571 --> 00:00:17,689
blink, and miss the whole arc.

9
00:00:17,729 --> 00:00:19,631
You never see the ball fly.

10
00:00:19,671 --> 00:00:22,076
You only ever see the ball arrive,

11
00:00:22,116 --> 00:00:22,867
or fail to.

12
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:25,400
Cooking becomes risky.

13
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:27,106
Blink, the toast is golden.

14
00:00:27,146 --> 00:00:28,433
Blink, it's charcoal.

15
00:00:28,473 --> 00:00:31,150
Blink again, and the smoke alarm is singing

16
00:00:31,190 --> 00:00:32,224
a very high note.

17
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:35,107
So you try never to blink.

18
00:00:35,147 --> 00:00:37,803
Staring contests become your new sport.

19
00:00:37,843 --> 00:00:40,222
But your eyes dry out like raisins,

20
00:00:40,262 --> 00:00:42,987
and your best friend tells jokes just to

21
00:00:43,027 --> 00:00:44,024
make you crack.

22
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:46,805
Do the math, hypothetically.

23
00:00:46,845 --> 00:00:50,223
About fifteen blinks a minute means fifteen seconds skipped.

24
00:00:50,263 --> 00:00:52,331
That's a quarter of your waking life,

25
00:00:52,371 --> 00:00:54,496
gone before you even finish breakfast.

26
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:59,258
At your birthday, you blink while blowing out the candles.

27
00:00:59,298 --> 00:01:00,641
The party jumps ahead.

28
00:01:00,681 --> 00:01:01,711
The cake is gone,

29
00:01:01,751 --> 00:01:03,346
the balloons are drooping,

30
00:01:03,386 --> 00:01:05,610
and everyone has politely gone home.

31
00:01:06,850 --> 00:01:08,340
But here's the twist.

32
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:11,253
A night of sleep is just one long blink.

33
00:01:11,293 --> 00:01:14,094
You'd wake up exactly one second later,

34
00:01:14,134 --> 00:01:17,153
rested, and the world would not have moved

35
00:01:17,193 --> 00:01:17,881
on at all.

36
00:01:19,150 --> 00:01:20,651
So you sit on a bench,

37
00:01:20,691 --> 00:01:23,382
close your eyes, and let the whole city

38
00:01:23,422 --> 00:01:25,342
stand still for a heartbeat.

39
00:01:25,382 --> 00:01:26,673
When you open them,

40
00:01:26,713 --> 00:01:29,404
the sunset has painted everything gold.

41
00:01:29,444 --> 00:01:29,824
Blink.
